Let an element compete for a touch drag that it wins once the touch passes the drag's slop, as Flutter's tap-and-drag
recognizers do, instead of only claiming it at touch down.

What: `Window::compete_for_touch_drag(kind)`, called from a listener of the touch-down offer (the `Started`
`TouchDragEvent`), enters the drag in the touch's arena without claiming it. The touch stays a tap, long press or pan
to be; on each move the competing drag runs first (Flutter routes the deeper recognizer first, so on a move both accept
the drag wins) and wins when its travel passes its kind's slop: `TouchDragKind::Horizontal`
(`TapAndHorizontalDragGestureRecognizer`: the signed horizontal travel past the hit slop) or `TouchDragKind::Pan`
(`TapAndPanGestureRecognizer`: the travel along the path past the pan slop), from `gpui::slops` and the window's
`GestureTuning::touch_slop`. It then streams `TouchDragEvent`s (`Started` at the touch's position, moves, end) like a
claimed drag, and the touch is the drag's: no tap, long press, pan or pinch. A drag that loses (a tap, a claimed long
press, the pan, a scroll hold) gets no event. `TouchDragEvent` gains `start: TouchDragStart` (`Down`: offered at touch
down, claimed with `prevent_default`; `PastSlop(kind)`: won by competing), so a listener tells the offer from the win.
The recognizer's pending touch holds the offer as one enum (`TouchDragOffer`: not offered, offered, competing with
Flutter's `_globalDistanceMoved`), replacing its `touch_drag_offered` flag. The acceptance rule
(`TouchDragKind::global_distance_moved`, `has_sufficient_global_distance_to_accept`) is ported near-verbatim from
Flutter's tap_and_drag.dart @ 3.50.1 (`BaseTapAndDragGestureRecognizer._checkDrag` and the two subclasses'
`_getDeltaForDetails`, `_getPrimaryValueFromOffset`, `_hasSufficientGlobalDistanceToAccept`). Dropped: the
`_wonArenaForPrimaryPointer && _globalDistanceMovedAllAxes > panSlop` clause (GPUI's pan always competes, so the drag
never wins an arena by default), `eagerVictoryOnDrag: false`, consecutive tap counts (a drag after a double tap),
`onTapDown` / `onCancel` callbacks, drag update throttling.

The pan follows the scroll containers under the touch, as Flutter's scrollables each add their drag recognizer: a div
that scrolls reports its axes while the touch's `Started` is dispatched (`Window::scroll_container_under_touch`, next
to `hold_scroll`), the touch route joins them (`PanAxes`: no container, one axis, both), and the recognizer's pending
touch accepts its pan by them. Only containers on one axis: the travel along that axis past the hit slop, monodrag.dart's
`VerticalDragGestureRecognizer` / `HorizontalDragGestureRecognizer._hasSufficientGlobalDistanceToAccept`, and the pan
locks to that axis. No container, a two-axis one or both kinds: the pan rule as before (any direction past the touch
slop, locked to the dominant axis). `list()` reports no axes (it does not take part in touch routing).

Why: a text field must keep its taps (caret) and long presses (word selection) while a horizontal finger drag moves
its caret, as Flutter's `TextSelectionGestureDetector` does on Android. GPUI's touch drag could only be claimed at
touch down, which takes the touch away from the tap and long-press recognizers, so Parallax's selection engine
(parallax-ext's text_selection, which already has Flutter's finger-drag caret move) could not get finger drags.
Without the container's axes, the pan took every move past 18 px in any direction, so on desktop rows a field's
`TouchDragKind::Pan` drag (36 px pan slop) never won inside a vertical list.

Test: `gestures::recognizer_tests::flutter_recognizer_tests_pass` gains 6 rows from tap_and_drag_test.dart (GPUI's pan
stands in for the test's `VerticalDragGestureRecognizer` or `PanGestureRecognizer`: horizontal drag beats it on a
horizontal drag and loses on a vertical one; the same for a pan; self-victory past the pan slop; a tap within the
slop stays a tap) and 4 GPUI rows for a text field's pair (claimed long press plus competing horizontal drag): the
horizontal travel adds up across moves, a diagonal move is the pan's before the horizontal slop, a tap stays a tap, a
long press held past its deadline beats the drag. Rows gain a `container`: the tap_and_drag_test.dart rows run in a
vertical container (their `VerticalDragGestureRecognizer`), drag_test.dart's horizontal-drag-with-competitor rows in a
horizontal one; 2 monodrag rows (a one-axis container's pan accepts only on its axis) and a GPUI row (a Pan-kind field
drag in a vertical list wins a horizontal drag). Run: `scripts/patch-test.sh recognizer`.

Upstream: not filed (patch rule 14).

